# Next.js 14 + Tailwind CSS Development Guide

You are an expert in TypeScript, Next.js 14 App Router, and Tailwind CSS.

## Core Rules
1. Use the App Router — all components inside `app/` directory
2. Server Components by default — Client Components only when needed for interactivity
3. Modern TypeScript syntax — proper typing for all components and functions
4. Tailwind CSS only for styling — no inline styles or CSS modules unless necessary
5. Responsive design — mobile-first Tailwind classes on every component

## Architecture
- Implement efficient data fetching, caching, and revalidation
- Use environment variables for all configuration
- Code splitting, lazy loading, and parallel data fetching where appropriate
- SEO best practices and metadata management on every page

## File Structure
- Lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., `components/auth-wizard`)
- Named exports for components
- Types and interfaces in separate `/types` files